        prompts: {
          human: "3-2-5 (Teen Do Panch, also 2-3-5 or 5-3-2) is a trick-taking card game played in India, Pakistan, and Nepal. Three players use a 30-card deck. Each has a trick quota: dealer 2, player to dealer's right 5, player to dealer's left 3. The 5-trick player chooses trump and leads. Players above quota can 'pull' cards from those below in the next deal.",
